/-! # Finite extensions of a DVR completion descend

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 09EJ
(lemma-approximate-separable-extension) and Tag 09F9 (theorem-epp), completion paragraph.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-dvr-completion-extension-approximation).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w z

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace IsDiscreteValuationRing

/-- A finite extension of the completed fraction field descends if it is separable,
or in positive characteristic if it is a compositum of a separable extension and
an extension generated by a prescribed power root of the original uniformizer.
The fraction-field maps agree on `A` by `hcompat`, so the map `F → K` is canonical.
The intermediate fields and the root are all inside the given field `H`.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tags 09EJ and 09F9 (completion paragraph).
(blueprint: lem-sfb-dvr-completion-extension-approximation).

Proof:
1. Write C for the maximal-ideal completion and K for its fraction field. By
   lem-weil-pbc-completion-of-dvr-is-dvr, C is a DVR. Its maximal ideal is generated
   by the image of pi (lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-local-ring). Completeness and
   C/(pi^n) = A/(pi^n) follow from lem-weil-pbc-module-completion-complete.
2. For a finite separable E/K choose a primitive element theta using
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-separable-extension-primitive-element. Scale theta by a power
   of pi so its monic minimal polynomial P has coefficients in C. Division by P
   identifies B = C[theta] with C[T]/(P); lem-weil-pbc-monic-quotient-free gives
   the basis 1, theta, ..., theta^(d-1).
3. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-complete-local-product, B is a complete Noetherian
   local domain. Integrality (lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral) and
   lem-weil-pbc-integral-extension-dimension give dimension at most one. Its
   nonzero nonunit pi gives dimension one. Separability gives P'(theta) nonzero.
   Apply lem-sfb-complete-local-domain-root-perturbation with t = pi and c = 1.
   Lift P's lower coefficients to A to the required precision, leaving it monic,
   to obtain P1 and a root beta in B with beta - theta in pi B.
4. The powers of beta span B/pi B. By lem-weil-pbc-nakayama-local-generators they
   span B. Evaluation gives a surjection C[T]/(P1) → B between free modules of the
   same rank. Its determinant is a unit, hence it is an isomorphism. Inverting pi
   gives K[T]/(P1) ≃ E.
5. Thus P1 is irreducible over K and over F. Put N0 = F[T]/(P1). By
   lem-weil-pbc-algebra-tensor-pushout-universal-property its base change is E.
   The derivative of P1 is nonzero since E/K is separable, hence it is nonzero
   over F. By lem-trf-irreducible-separable-derivative and
   lem-trf-simple-separable-field-extension, N0/F is finite separable. This proves
   the separable case, including the conditional separability in the conclusion.
6. In the other case set q = p^r and L = F(alpha). The root algebras over A and C
   are domains by lem-sbc-dvr-uniformizer-root-algebra. Invert pi; the resulting
   finite-dimensional domains are fields and evaluation at the same alpha embeds
   them into H. Their degree-q bases come from lem-weil-pbc-monic-quotient-free.
   The tensor universal property gives K ⊗[F] L ≃ K(alpha), preserving alpha.
   Frobenius shows these root extensions are purely inseparable, also when r = 0.
7. Apply steps 2--5 to M and embed N0 into M using its tensor isomorphism.
   By lem-weil-pbc-separable-purely-inseparable-linear-disjoint, multiplication
   identifies N0 ⊗[F] L with the compositum N0 L, a finite-dimensional field N.
   The same result over K identifies M ⊗[K] K(alpha) with H. Tensor associativity
   and the universal property identify K ⊗[F] N with H. On pure tensors the
   reassociation sends c ⊗ (n ⊗ l) to (c ⊗ n) ⊗ (1 ⊗ l); the inverse multiplies
   the two K-coefficients. Thus the prescribed root is unchanged throughout.
-/
theorem exists_finite_extension_tensor_equiv
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    (F : Type v) [Field F] [Algebra A F] [IsFractionRing A F]
    (pi : A) (hpi : Irreducible pi)
    (K : Type w) [Field K]
    [Algebra (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) K]
    [Algebra F K]
    (hcompat : ∀ a : A, algebraMap F K (algebraMap A F a) =
      algebraMap (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) K
        (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) a))
    (H : Type z) [Field H] [Algebra K H] [FiniteDimensional K H]
    (hH : Algebra.IsSeparable K H ∨
      ∃ (p r : ℕ) (M : IntermediateField K H) (alpha : H),
        0 < p ∧ CharP F p ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable K M ∧
        alpha ^ (p ^ r) = algebraMap K H
          (algebraMap (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) K
            (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) pi)) ∧
        M ⊔ IntermediateField.adjoin K {alpha} = ⊤) :
    ∃ (N : Type v) (_ : Field N) (_ : Algebra F N),
      FiniteDimensional F N ∧ Nonempty ((K ⊗[F] N) ≃ₐ[K] H) ∧
        (Algebra.IsSeparable K H → Algebra.IsSeparable F N) := by
  sorry

end IsDiscreteValuationRing
